Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: guard segment-end notification for audio-only sources

An audio-only presentation has no video frame sink. The segment-end event
currently passes NULL into a helper that unconditionally writes sink->eos.
Guard that call and hold engine->cs while borrowing its presentation sink,
matching original Proton-RTSP's MediaEngine event handler.

The lock also prevents concurrent source teardown from freeing this borrowed
pointer during the call. It does not attribute a stale session event to a
source generation. Do not add redundant caller checks around the already
NULL-safe get_sample/reset helpers. Independent of 0033/0034; apply after SE1.
Extracted-case tests are not actual MF session or audio-only playback proof.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1264,7 +1264,10 @@
             break;
 
         case MEEndOfPresentationSegment:
-            video_frame_sink_notify_end_of_presentation_segment(engine->presentation.frame_sink);
+            EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
+            if (engine->presentation.frame_sink)
+                video_frame_sink_notify_end_of_presentation_segment(engine->presentation.frame_sink);
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
             break;
 
         case MESessionRateChanged:
